  "problem": "Which statement is **not** true?",
  "worked_solution": "If $A\u2286B,$ then $A$ is a subset of $B,$ meaning that every element of $A$ is an element of $B.$\n\nAmong the given choices, only ${Z}^{-}\u2286N$ is not true. This statement is not true because not every negative integer is a natural number. For example, we have $-1\\in {Z}^{-}$ but $-1\\notin N.$",
